But I Would Change One Thing


I would not buy six GPU servers with two RTX PRO 6000s each simply because we can.


The RTX PRO 6000 has 96 GB ECC GDDR7 and NVIDIA's current listed price is $13,250 per card. 


For NEXUS, GPU workloads are heterogeneous:


ENTITY RESOLUTION
      ↓
EMBEDDINGS
      ↓
VISION
      ↓
LLM INFERENCE
      ↓
SPATIAL COMPUTATION
      ↓
SIMULATION
      ↓
GPU PROJECTION



Some workloads benefit enormously from VRAM; others don't.


So I'd initially build:


GPU pool


4 × high-VRAM professional GPUs


8 × high-performance consumer/prosumer GPUs


rather than 12 identical professional cards.


That gives NEXUS a much better price/performance envelope.



