The important financial insight


Don't try to purchase the final planetary computer at the beginning.


Build NEXUS as a scale-out system.


The first cluster should prove:




Can NEXUS correctly represent, reconstruct, query, verify, and visualize a changing world?




Once that works, adding:


10× compute, 10× storage, 10× ingestion, 10× geographic coverage


should primarily mean adding nodes—not rewriting the architecture.


That is what turns the ~$2.5M Phase 1 platform into a credible foundation rather than an expensive one-off supercomputer.

